{"text": "\u2018State of Calfomia\u2014Transportation Agency\n\nDEPARTMENT OF CALIFORNIA HIGHWAY PATROL,\nOFFICE OF RISK MANAGEMENT\nPublic Records Unit\nPO Box 842898\n\u2018Sacramento, CA 94298-0001\n(916) 843-4030\n(800) 735-2829 (TT/TDD)\n(800) 738-2822 (Voice)\n\nJuly 8, 2019\nFile No.: 033,15087.A13429,2022.06.221\n\nMuckRoock News\nDEPT MR 72094\n411A Highland Avenue\n\u2018Somerville, MA 02144-2516\n\n\u2018To whom it may concem:\n\n\u2018The Califomia Highway Patrol, Office of Community Outreach and Media Relations, received your\nCalifornia Public Records Act request, dated May 12, 2019, and received on May 13, 2019, which was\n\u2018subsequently forwarded to the Office of Risk Management, Public Records Unit (PRU).\n\n\u2018On May 23, 2019, PRU notified you, in writing, personnel were determining if the Department possessed\npublic records responsive to your request, which would require them to search for and collect the\nrequested records from facilites separate from the office processing the request. Accordingly, PRU\n\u2018extended the 10-day response timeframe, by an additional 14 days, as authorized by California\n\u2018Government Code 6253, subdivision (c)(1). Please accept this notification of PRU's determination\nregarding your request.\n\nIn your request you asked for the following, verbatim:\n\n\u2018\u00a9 The responsive records for your PRA File# 033, 15087.16753.2022.01.136. We don't need the\nrequest or response letters/emails or the identity of the requestor - just the responsive records.\nPRU responded to your request, in writing, on June 6, 2019, advising you there were records responsive\nto your request. This letter wll confirm our receipt of your payment, in the amount of $20.00, which will\n\u2018cover the Department's costs in duplicating these records on (4) four CD's and has been enclosed.\n\nIfyou have any questions of you need additional information, please contact any member of the Public\nRecords Unit, at (916) \u20ac43-4030,\n\nSincerely,\n\nJ.R-DOLCE, Captain\n\u2018Commander\nOffice of Risk Management\n\nSafety, Service, and Security & An Internationally Accredited Agency",
